# ELECTRICAL FIRE WITH SMOKE in flight (format 1). The checklist is reproduced as printed in the DA50 C / RG Emergency Procedures checklist, Edition 4.1 of 2022-10-05 (owner decisions 2026-10-23 and 2026-10-27): the heading, both WARNING blocks, every item, action and sub-heading as printed. The row marks are the letters A to H of the AFM page that was compared. ASSUMPTION for the owner: the booklet may print numbers 1 to 8 instead; the marks are plain data (the `number` fields), so swapping them is one edit per row plus the typed table in tests/checklist-reference.ts. The Emergency Windows row is an optional step on the window (printed "if required"); the Doors row is an optional step on the door release lever (the simulation has no landing, so the rows below the sub-heading may be done at any time and are credited whenever the door opens); the precautionary landing and the evacuation have no panel action and stay lines. All other text is own wording. The smoke source, the outcome threshold and hold time and the onset window are instructor-review values.
format: 1
id: elec-fire-flight
title: ELEC FIRE FLIGHT
source:
  document: "DA50 C / RG Emergency Procedures checklist"
  issue: "Edition 4.1, 2022-10-05"
  section: AFM 03-34 ELECTRICAL FIRE WITH SMOKE IN FLIGHT
  verified: "2026-10-27"
disclaimer: training-aid
scene: cruise
briefing:
  situation: "You are in cruise flight when you smell burning plastic and smoke fills the cabin. No message is shown on the primary flight display. The smoke is getting thicker and its source seems to be electrical. The cabin air is set to recirculate."
initial:
  controls:
    lv.env_circ: recirc
  quantities:
    smoke_density: 40
parameters:
  smoke_source: 1
annunciations[0]:
checklist:
  form: table
  heading: Electrical Fire in Flight
procedure[11]:
  - kind: comment
    style: warning
    text: "IN THE EVENT OF SMOKE OR FIRE, PREPARE TO LAND THE AIRPLANE WITHOUT DELAY WHILE COMPLETING FIRE SUPPRESSION AND/OR SMOKE EVACUATION PROCEDURES. IF IT CANNOT BE VISUALLY VERIFIED THAT THE FIRE HAS BEEN COMPLETELY EXTINGUISHED, WHETHER THE SMOKE HAS CLEARED OR NOT, LAND IMMEDIATELY."
  - kind: group
    id: grp_av_master
    ordered: false
    steps[1]:
      - id: av_master_off
        severity: critical
        number: A
        text: AVIONIC MASTER
        action: "OFF"
        done:
          check: state
          control: sw.av_master
          is: off
  - kind: comment
    style: warning
    text: "SWITCHING OFF THE ELECT. MASTER WILL LEAD TO TOTAL FAILURE OF ALL ELECTRONIC AND ELECTRIC EQUIPMENT."
  - kind: group
    id: grp_elect_master
    ordered: false
    steps[1]:
      - id: elect_master_off
        severity: critical
        number: B
        text: ELECT. MASTER
        action: "OFF"
        done:
          check: state
          control: sw.elect_master
          is: off
  - kind: group
    id: grp_circ_air
    ordered: false
    steps[1]:
      - id: circ_air_fresh
        severity: critical
        number: C
        text: CIRCULATING AIR
        action: FRESH AIR
        done:
          check: state
          control: lv.env_circ
          is: fresh
  - kind: group
    id: grp_ecs_pull
    ordered: false
    steps[1]:
      - id: ecs_pulled
        severity: critical
        number: D
        text: ECS shut-off
        action: PULL
        done:
          check: state
          control: lv.ecs_shutoff
          is: pulled
  - kind: group
    id: grp_windows
    ordered: false
    steps[1]:
      - id: windows_open
        severity: optional
        number: E
        text: Emergency Windows
        action: OPEN if required
        done:
          check: state
          control: sw.emerg_window
          is: open
  - kind: line
    number: F
    text: Perform a precautionary landing on the nearest airfield.
  - kind: comment
    style: subheading
    text: When Airplane Has Stopped
  - kind: group
    id: grp_doors
    ordered: false
    steps[1]:
      - id: doors_open
        severity: optional
        number: G
        text: Doors
        action: open
        done:
          check: state
          control: lv.door_release
          is: open
  - kind: line
    number: H
    text: Airplane
    action: evacuate immediately
# The outcome ends the run as a fail when the cabin stays full of smoke; the density and the hold time are instructor-review values.
outcomes[1]:
  - id: cabin_smoke_full
    text: Cabin full of smoke
    hold_s: 30
    when:
      check: quantity
      quantity: smoke_density
      op: gte
      value: 95
# The smoke of the level Realistic begins at a random second inside this short window; the window is an instructor-review value.
# The smoke shows over the panel, since the scenario lists no message; the lint checks that it shows within seconds of the onset.
onset:
  window_s[2]: 2,6
  cues[1]: cabin_smoke
